        446.61968994140625,
        522.0006103515625,
        456.3724060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which is precisely the result of Theorem 3.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00006103515625,
        474.9096984863281,
        276.6329345703125,
        484.66241455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B.2. Proof that Split Conformal Prediction Reduces to Robust Scenario Optimization",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        514.8037109375,
        486.98199462890625,
        524.6110229492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Here, we show that split conformal prediction, in full generality, reduces to a robust scenario opti-",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        534.2676391601562,
        522.0000610351562,
        544.0203857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mization problem. We hope that this insight will encourage future research on the close relationship",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        547.817626953125,
        522.0000610351562,
        557.5703735351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "between the highly related but disparate fields of conformal prediction and scenario optimization.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        561.3666381835938,
        522.0001220703125,
        571.119384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In split conformal prediction, we first define a score function s(x, y) ∈R which is meant to reflect",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        574.1301879882812,
        522.0001831054688,
        584.6683959960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the uncertainty for a model input x and corresponding model output y. Then, we sample an i.i.d.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        588.2900390625,
        521.9959716796875,
        598.2173461914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "calibration set (X1, Y1), ..., (Xn, Yn) and compute ˆq as the ⌈(n+1)(1−α)⌉",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        599.2194213867188,
        404.660888671875,
        613.7532348632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "n",
      "bbox": [
        375.6340026855469,
        608.8017578125,
        380.77471923828125,
        615.8792114257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "quantile of the calibration",
      "bbox": [
        408.8380126953125,
        603.1746215820312,
        521.9979248046875,
        612.9273681640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "scores s(X1, Y1), ..., s(Xn, Yn), where α ∈[0, 1] is a user-chosen error rate. For a new i.i.d. sample",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        615.9381713867188,
        521.9981079101562,
        627.3031616210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xtest, we construct a prediction set C(Xtest) = {y : s(Xtest, y) ≤ˆq}. Theorem 1 in Angelopoulos",
      "bbox": [
        90.00001525878906,
        629.4871826171875,
        521.9995727539062,
        641.0275268554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and Bates (2023) provides the following coverage property: P (Ytest ∈C(Xtest)) ≥1 −α. This",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        643.0371704101562,
        522.0030517578125,
        654.9713745117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "follows from the more powerful property, first introduced in Vovk (2012), which we prove reduces",
      "bbox": [
        90.00006103515625,
        657.3716430664062,
        522.0003662109375,
        667.1243896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to a robust scenario-based result after:",
      "bbox": [
        90.00006103515625,
        670.920654296875,
        256.1020202636719,
        680.6734008789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "P (Ytest ∈C(Xtest)|{(Xi, Yi)}n",
      "bbox": [
        142.36306762695312,
        692.8257446289062,
        278.5407409667969,
        706.6143798828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1) ∼Beta(n + 1 −l, l),",
      "bbox": [
        273.4000244140625,
        694.68017578125,
        388.3607482910156,
        707.1051635742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "l = ⌊(n + 1)α⌋",
      "bbox": [
        401.0916748046875,
        694.68017578125,
        469.63165283203125,
        704.9783935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
